            "desc": "No-op create. Zero arguments on purpose.\nThe 68-year trap: never take a uint64 create arg that a deploy script might map to the keeper app id. Nothing to pass here.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "set_keeper",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "keeper"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Name the Arcron keeper whose app account may call `tick`.\nCreator-only, one-time. Pass the keeper *application*, not a raw uint64. `tick` authorizes Application(keeper).address - the inner-call sender when Arcron `execute()` inner-calls this app - never itob(keeper.id). Puya lowers the Application param to uint64 in the ABI signature; the compiled selector is set_keeper(uint64)void.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "set_beneficiary",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "address",
                    "name": "beneficiary"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Name the account allowed to pull the allowance via `claim`.\nOwner-only, one-time. There is deliberately no re-point method: the stream pays whoever the owner named at the start, and a one-time name keeps that promise simple. Puya lowers the Account param to address in the ABI signature; the compiled selector is set_beneficiary(address)void.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "set_drip",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "drip"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Set (or re-set) the uALGO matured per keeper tick.\nOwner-only, re-settable: the owner may raise or lower the stream at will, floored at MIN_DRIP (1000 uALGO) so a claim's pooled fee never rivals the payout. Applies from the next `tick`; drips already matured keep paying out at whatever rate they matured.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "fund",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "pay",
                    "name": "payment"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Top up the pool. Anyone may fund; the money only ever flows\nout to the named beneficiary.\nThe payment must land on the app address and carry more than zero uALGO. Matured drips are only matured while the pool can cover them (see `tick`), so funding after the fact does not back-pay missed ticks - it just lets future ticks mature.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "tick",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Arcron hook. Zero arguments; the selector is the only app arg.\nReturns the new `matured` count when a drip matures, 0 on every no-work path. FAIL SOFT: after the two authorization asserts nothing here may reject - a failing hook gets exponentially backed off by keeper bots and burns upkeep escrow on retries.\nNo-work paths, all returning 0:   * beneficiary unset - a stream with nobody to pull it does not     mature;   * pool underfunded - the app balance minus the APP_MIN_BALANCE     floor (100000 uALGO) cannot cover drip * (matured + 1), so     one more drip would promise money the pool cannot pay.\nBest-effort, not catch-up: a missed or skipped tick is a missed drip. Register with SKIP_AHEAD; see README.md.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "claim",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Pull the matured allowance. Beneficiary-only.\nPays matured * drip uALGO out of the app balance with an inner payment, adds it to `claimed_total`, and zeroes `matured`. If nothing has matured, returns quietly (fail-soft; a no-op claim is harmless).\nFEE POOLING: the inner payment carries a 1000 uALGO fee, so the outer call must set a flat fee >= 2000 uALGO (1000 outer + 1000 inner). A claim sent with the default 1000 uALGO fee fails on fee underspend. This is the pull-payment trade the README calls out: one pooled fee, paid by the beneficiary, only when they actually pull.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "claimable",
            "args": [],
            "returns": {
                "type": "uint64"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": true,
            "desc": "uALGO the beneficiary could pull right now: matured * drip.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        }
    ],
